      "attrs": {
        "text": "You are reviewing one task's implementation: whether it matches its requirements, then whether it is well-built. Task-scoped gate, not a merge review.\n\n## What Was Requested\nRead the task brief: `/Users/sumandra/projects/talium/code-econ/.superpowers/sdd/task-4-brief.md`\n\nGlobal constraints that bind this task:\n- SQLAlchemy 2.0 typed declarative (`Mapped[...]` + `mapped_column`). Dumb models: NO `relationship()`, NO foreign keys anywhere.\n- `producers` has `record` JSONB plus STORED generated columns `key_hash`/`key_prefix` via `Computed(\"(record ->> '...')\", persisted=True)`, a UNIQUE index on `key_hash`, and an index on `key_prefix`.\n- `session_info.cost_usd` is `Numeric` (not str); map fields use the `jsb` alias, list fields (`skills`/`subagents`/`pr_list`) use the `jsl` alias. `sessions.agent` is a plain string (no FK to a lookup).\n- `Base.metadata` must contain exactly: producers, sessions, session_info, users. All timestamps timestamptz via the `ts` alias.\n- No \"Claude\" anywhere. TDD required.\n\n## Implementer Report\n`/Users/sumandra/projects/talium/code-econ/.superpowers/sdd/task-4-report.md` — treat as unverified claims.\n\n## Diff Under Review\nBase: 12d946b  Head: 95fea9a\nDiff file: `/Users/sumandra/projects/talium/code-econ/.superpowers/sdd/review-12d946b..95fea9a.diff`\nRead the diff file once. Do not re-run git or crawl the codebase. Read-only.\n\n## Tests\nImplementer reports 3 passing (metadata-only, no DB). Do not re-run the suite; a focused run only for a specific doubt. Warnings/noise are findings.\n\n## Part 1: Spec Compliance — Missing / Extra / Misunderstood vs. brief (check every model's fields, the generated columns, indexes, no-FK rule, Numeric cost, jsb/jsl usage).\n## Part 2: Code Quality — correctness of the Computed expressions and index definitions, alias usage, structure. Cite file:line.\n\n## Calibration\nSeverity by actual impact. Important = can't be trusted until fixed (e.g. a wrong Computed expression, a stray FK, cost as str). Polish = Minor. Plan-mandated defects → Important labeled plan-mandated. Acknowledge strengths.\n\n## Output Format\n### Spec Compliance — ✅ | ❌ (file:line) | ⚠️ Cannot verify\n### Strengths\n### Issues — Critical / Important / Minor (file:line, what, why, fix)\n### Assessment — **Task quality:** Approved | Needs fixes; **Reasoning:** 1-2 sentences.\nBegin directly with the spec-compliance verdict.",
